# Chaos engineering with stock OTP

```elixir
Mix.install([{:elixir_harness, path: "."}])
```

No chaos-monkey library. Three primitives:

- `Process.exit(pid, :kill)` on a permanent worker — the supervisor
  restarts it under the same `Registry` name. Callers see a new pid,
  never a dead name.
- `:sys.suspend/2` — freeze a worker, watch its caller time out, resume.
  The supervision equivalent of "what if this hangs in prod".
- `rest_for_one` — killing child `:b` restarts `:b` and everything after
  it (`:c`), never `:a`. Ordering as a strategy flag, not code.

```sh
mix showcase chaos
```

Strategy choice is the demo: `one_for_one` isolates (tools),
`rest_for_one` orders (pipelines). Pick per subtree.
